cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Lifeline: an offline, end-to-end-encrypted mesh messenger"
message: "If you use Lifeline or its protocol in your research, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Archit
    family-names: Sharma
    email: archit.sharma@nometria.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/matrix-share/matrix"
url: "https://matrix-alpha-ashen.vercel.app"
abstract: >-
  Lifeline is an open-source, self-hostable, end-to-end-encrypted mesh messenger
  that keeps people connected when the internet and cellular networks fail.
  Phones relay messages device-to-device using delay-tolerant store-carry-forward,
  with sealed-sender envelopes, forward secrecy, and cryptographic proof of
  delivery, and opportunistically bridge queued messages to the internet the
  moment any node regains connectivity.
keywords:
  - mesh networking
  - delay-tolerant networking
  - end-to-end encryption
  - offline-first
  - disaster response
  - decentralized messaging
license: Apache-2.0
